4:42Z","licenses":{"code":{"basis":"repository LICENSE header; not a weights/data license","declared":"Apache-2.0","retrieved_at":"2026-10-19T07:04:46Z","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/imoonkey/closepaw/HEAD/LICENSE"},"data":null,"document":null,"weights":null},"links":[{"rel":"primary","url":"https://github.com/imoonkey/closepaw"}],"name":"ClosePaw","notes":"Kotlin app for Android 12 or later with an on-device ReAct loop, subagent delegation, todo and scratchpad tools, markdown memory files and per-app skills. Perception defaults to the accessibility tree; screenshot-only and hybrid modes are options (perception/PerceptionConfig.kt). Clicks try an accessibility ACTION_CLICK on the resolved node and fall back to a dispatched gesture tap (tool/action/ClickExecutor.kt, platform/NodeActionPerformer.kt, platform/AccessibilityGestureInjector.kt). Optional power tools use Shizuku for a background virtual display, Termux for a Linux shell, and Chrome DevTools Protocol scripting of Chrome. A bundled tier list blocks banking, payment, crypto-wallet, password-manager and authenticator packages (assets/security/app_tiers.json), and other apps need per-app approval. Models are reached through OpenAI-compatible endpoints or a ChatGPT/Codex sign-in. The eval/ harness drives AndroidWorld task setup and scoring and launches the app over ADB.","published_at":null,"relations":[{"evidence_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/imoonkey/closepaw/75dae2653f5a6b25d5df51ee7008b0f830de1536/eval/README.md","target_id":"github:google-research/android_world","type":"uses"}],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"On-device Android agent app that reads the accessibility tree, with optional screenshots, acts through accessibility node actions or gesture taps, and can run on a Shizuku virtual display in the background.","topics":["mobile-navigation","human-in-the-loop","memory"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://github.com/imoonkey/closepaw"}
